---
import PropertyPackPage from '@/components/property-pack/PropertyPackPage.astro';
import { counts, candidateManifest } from '@/lib/property-pack-model.mjs';
---
<PropertyPackPage title="Property Pack" description="Understand the Property Pack, follow a worked example and review the proposed data model and its evidence.">
  <h1>Property Pack</h1>
  <p class="lead">A shared set of property information for a transaction. This section shows the proposed model for describing that information consistently, the evidence behind it and the decisions still needed.</p>

  <div class="pp-overview" id="what-it-is">
    <section>
      <h2>Give information a meaning people can share</h2>
      <p>A property transaction draws on information held by different people and organisations: identifiers, title information, certificates, searches and answers about the property.</p>
      <p>The Property Pack brings a defined selection together. The <strong>ontology</strong> is the model of what those things mean and how they connect, so an answer can be understood beyond the document or system it came from.</p>
      <p><a href="/development/property-pack/worked-example">See how an energy certificate connects to a property →</a></p>
    </section>
    <figure class="pp-pack">
      <figcaption>One pack, several kinds of evidence</figcaption>
      <ul><li>Which property? Identifiers and address</li><li>What is recorded? Title and legal information</li><li>What supports it? Certificates and search results</li><li>What is being reported? Property questions and answers</li></ul>
      <small>Illustrative information families. The exact current scope is the 451-row source catalogue.</small>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="reference">What would you like to do?</h2>
  <div class="pp-paths">
    <a class="pp-path" href="/development/property-pack/definition-and-scope"><span class="pp-path__role">New to the work</span><h3>Understand the pack and the 451 items</h3><p>What is included, where the number comes from and why required information can be conditional.</p><strong>Start with the scope →</strong></a>
    <a class="pp-path" href="/development/property-pack/work-packages"><span class="pp-path__role">Property practitioners and contributors</span><h3>Review a familiar topic</h3><p>Choose a slice such as property identity, legal information or energy. Check the wording against your experience.</p><strong>Choose a review topic →</strong></a>
    <a class="pp-path" href="/development/property-pack/model"><span class="pp-path__role">Modellers and implementers</span><h3>Explore the candidate model</h3><p>Understand contexts, browse terms and relationships, then inspect value lists and validation rules.</p><strong>Read the model guide →</strong></a>
    <a class="pp-path" href="/development/property-pack/technical-working-group-determination"><span class="pp-path__role">Reviewers and decision makers</span><h3>Check readiness and the next decision</h3><p>Separate generated evidence from human agreement, release and authority.</p><strong>Open the review status →</strong></a>
  </div>

  <h2 id="headline-counts">What is available today?</h2>
  <ol class="pp-sequence">
    <li><span class="pill pill--info">Source evidence</span><h3>{counts.sourceItems} source items</h3><p>The exact workbook rows selected as Required, with paths, conditions and provenance. <a href="/development/property-pack/data-dictionary">Find an item</a>.</p></li>
    <li><span class="pill pill--warn">Candidate model</span><h3>{counts.resources} model terms</h3><p>Proposed classes and properties, with source traces, {counts.schemes} value lists and {counts.shapes} validation shapes. <a href="/development/property-pack/resources">Browse the terms</a>.</p></li>
    <li><span class="pill pill--warn">Decision pending</span><h3>Human review remains open</h3><p>The recorded candidate is {candidateManifest.candidate_version}. No Technical Working Group determination or SPDTF release is recorded. <a href="/development/property-pack/technical-working-group-determination">See what remains</a>.</p></li>
  </ol>
  <p class="pp-source-note">The original determination target was 30 September 2026. It remains a historical target; this site does not record its completion or invent a replacement date.</p>

  <h2 id="scope">Where this fits in SPDTF</h2>
  <p>The <strong>Smart Property Data Trust Framework (SPDTF)</strong> is the wider collaborative scheme being developed. The Property Pack candidate is one component. The existing <strong>PDTF JSON schema</strong> and the separate <strong>ontology derived from that schema</strong> are evidence inputs with their own histories.</p>
  <p><a href="/development/property-pack/pdtf-schema-lineage">Compare the three artefacts and their evidence →</a></p>
  <h2 id="boundaries">Who understands each part?</h2>
  <p>Conveyancing, estate agency, finance, surveying, property-data services and property technology each bring their own language and expertise. The model gives each term a proposed <strong>semantic home</strong>, so its meaning can be reviewed in the right context.</p>
  <p><a href="/development/property-pack/contexts">Understand the context boundaries</a> or <a href="/development/property-pack/work-packages">start with a practical review topic</a>.</p>
</PropertyPackPage>
